(A) GEOMETRIC metrics: monotone in circular distance d -> SAME tournament
========================================================================
   d     tropical(gap)  quantum-fid  Galois-chord  quasicrystal(agree)
   0.02   0.020         0.998        0.126         50.00
   0.10   0.100         0.951        0.618         10.00
   0.20   0.200         0.809        1.176         5.00
   0.30   0.300         0.588        1.618         3.33
   0.40   0.400         0.309        1.902         2.50
   0.50   0.500         0.000        2.000         2.00
   => tropical(up), chord(up), quasicrystal-agreement(down), fidelity(down):
      all STRICTLY MONOTONE in d, so the threshold-tie tournament is identical
      to the standard circular runner tournament. GEOMETRIC = collapse.

========================================================================
(B) p-ADIC ULTRAMETRIC trienerment (ARITHMETIC, NEW): isosceles + sieve-LRC
========================================================================
   n=6, p=3, K=1 (d_p tie iff p^1|(v_i-v_j)): ultrametric isosceles law holds=True; observer-tie-free == sieve(no mult of 3): 300/301 (obs-tie-free in 44)
   n=6, p=2, K=2 (d_p tie iff p^2|(v_i-v_j)): ultrametric isosceles law holds=True; observer-tie-free == sieve(no mult of 4): 300/301 (obs-tie-free in 70)
   n=18, p=3, K=2 (d_p tie iff p^2|(v_i-v_j)): ultrametric isosceles law holds=True; observer-tie-free == sieve(no mult of 9): 300/301 (obs-tie-free in 42)
   => the p-adic metric is an ULTRAMETRIC (every triangle isosceles) -> a TREE;
      its trienerment ties = same p-adic ball = same channel (S533/S534); observer
      tie-free = the SIEVE (THM-369, lonely at t=1/p^K). Genuinely new (arithmetic).

========================================================================
(C) GRUNDY game-tournament (ARITHMETIC, NEW): periodicity = arithmetic structure
========================================================================
   subtraction set S=(1, 2): Grundy eventual period = 3; head = [0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2]
   subtraction set S=(2, 3): Grundy eventual period = 5; head = [0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 0, 1, 1]
   subtraction set S=(1, 3, 4): Grundy eventual period = 7; head = [0, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 0, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 0, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 0, 1, 0]
   subtraction set S=(3, 5): Grundy eventual period = 8; head = [0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2]
   => each pair's game has Grundy period tied to the speeds; the game-tournament
      (i beats j iff combined game is an N-position) is arithmetic; tie = P-position;
      LRC observer = a balanced P-position. Lives on the difference/nim structure.

========================================================================
(D) ZETA orbit-lengths (ARITHMETIC): pairwise periods = |v_i-v_j| (the differences)
========================================================================
   v=(1, 2, 3, 4): pairwise orbit-lengths |v_i-v_j| = [1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3] (the holdback atoms, S25)
   v=(1, 3, 7, 11): pairwise orbit-lengths |v_i-v_j| = [2, 4, 4, 6, 8, 10] (the holdback atoms, S25)

========================================================================
DICHOTOMY: GEOMETRIC metrics (tropical/quantum/sandpile/quasicrystal/Galois-chord)
collapse to the circular distance => the standard runner tournament. ARITHMETIC
metrics (p-adic ultrametric / Grundy / zeta-orbit / Galois-Frobenius) are functions
of the DIFFERENCES v_i-v_j => new tournaments on the difference/channel structure
(S533/S538). The genuinely new tournament content is ARITHMETIC, not geometric.
========================================================================
